    "answer": {
      "short": "All five curves have period $2\\pi$. Their ranges are $[-1,1]$, $[0,2]$, $[-2,0]$, $[0,4]$ and $[-3,-1]$, respectively.",
      "worked": "Use the sine key values $0,1,0,-1,0$ at $x=0,\\frac\\pi2,\\pi,\\frac{3\\pi}2,2\\pi$. The corresponding ordinates are:\n\n$y=\\sin x$: $0,1,0,-1,0$;\n\n$y=\\sin x+1$: $1,2,1,0,1$;\n\n$y=\\sin x-1$: $-1,0,-1,-2,-1$;\n\n$y=2\\sin x+2$: $2,4,2,0,2$;\n\n$y=\\sin x-2$: $-2,-1,-2,-3,-2$.\n\nPlot and join each set smoothly on common axes.",
      "solutionDiagrams": [
